    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Junior Caminero** headlines the Zurich Zebras lineup as our strongest play with a 77.68 efficiency score. His matchup against Mason Barnett is bolstered by a +10% park factor and the high-leverage utility of the #3 spot in the order, where he is well-positioned to capitalize on run-production opportunities. Close behind, **Yordan Alvarez** (71.23) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.59) remain essential starts; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** specifically provides critical speed to address our scarcity in stolen bases, while **Yordan Alvarez** offers elite power production despite his neutral venue. **Lars Nootbaar** also grades out as a top-tier option (67.77) thanks to a favorable matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano and a robust +19% SP skill advantage.\n\nStrategic platoon edges and situational dynamics heavily influenced our roster construction. **Christian Yelich** earns a strong 65.65 score, elevated by a significant +13% dynamic platoon boost against Walker Buehler. Meanwhile, **Trea Turner** (65.12) is locked in not only for his offensive consistency but for the +4% efficiency bump derived from the slow delivery of Andre Pallante, which enhances his stolen base potential\u2014a key priority for our 5x5 objectives. While **Nelson Velazquez** (51.90) provides solid value, his ceiling is slightly suppressed by a lower base projection relative to our primary starters. \n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins involved **Carson Benge**, who finished with a 50.14 score. While he remains a viable depth piece, he was edged out of the active lineup by the superior efficiency and platoon alignment of **Chase Meidroth** (57.36). While **Carson Benge** offers upside, his -9% hit from a same-handed platoon disadvantage against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez made him the logical omission for today\u2019s constraints. We are closely monitoring the lineup postings for **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, and the rest of the squad; as most of our core is currently listed as \"Lineup Pending,\" any drastic shifts in batting order\u2014particularly for **Kyle Schwarber** or **Colt Keith**\u2014could require late adjustments to preserve our game caps if the projected efficiency metrics crater.",
